# E2E Cucumber Conventions

## Feature File Structure

- One feature per file, scoped to a single user journey
- Use `Scenario` (not `Scenario Outline`) for distinct flows
- Each scenario should be independently runnable — include all prerequisites in `Given`

```gherkin
Feature: User Registration
    As a user
    I want to be able to register to the application
    So that I can add my income and get paid

    Scenario: Complete individual registration and reach the dashboard
        Given I am logged in and on the registration page
        When I fill in first name "E2E" and last name "Test"
        And I fill in bank account name "ทดสอบ อี ทู อี"
        And I select bank "ttb"
        And I fill in bank account number "1234567890"
        And I fill in phone "0812345678"
        And I fill in slack account "e2etest@oddsteam.com"
        And I select user type "individual"
        And I select a site
        And I upload the ID card PDF
        And I click the save button
        Then I should be on the individual dashboard
```

## Step Definitions (`e2e/cucumber/steps/*.steps.ts`)

- Use `chromium` via Playwright; `browser` and `page` live in `Before`/`After` hooks
- `APP_URL` is `http://localhost:4200`
- Keycloak runs at `localhost:9000`; credentials are `e2e` / `s3cr3t`
- For file upload steps, reference fixtures from `e2e/cucumber/fixtures/`

```typescript
// Login helper pattern (reused in Given steps that require auth)
await page.goto(`${APP_URL}/login`);
await page.getByText("Login with Keycloak").click();
await page.waitForURL(/localhost:9000/);
await page.locator("#username").fill("e2e");
await page.locator("#password").fill("s3cr3t");
await page.locator("#kc-login").click();
await page.waitForURL((url) => !url.pathname.includes("/login"), { timeout: 15000 });
```

## Registration Flow

After login, new users land on `/firstlogin`. The form fields and their selectors:

| Field | Selector |
|---|---|
| First Name | `#FirstName` |
| Last Name | `#LastName` |
| Bank Account Name | `#bankAccountName` |
| Bank | `#bankCode` (select) |
| Bank Account Number | `#bankAccountNumber` |
| Phone | `#phone` |
| Slack Account | `#slackAccount` |
| User Type (role) | `#role` (select: `individual` or `corporate`) |
| Site | `#siteId` (select first non-empty option) |
| ID Card PDF | `input[type="file"]` — use `setInputFiles()` |

After submit with `role=individual` → redirected to `/individual`.

## Fixtures

Place test files in `e2e/cucumber/fixtures/`. Example: `test-idcard.pdf` for the ID card upload step.

## Running Tests

```bash
make e2e          # run all scenarios
make e2e ARGS="--tags @tag"  # run tagged scenarios
```
